[[File:Pokok pecah beling (Strobilanthes crispa) 1.jpg|thumb|right|Leaves]]
'''''Strobilanthes crispa''''' is a shrub which originated from [[Madagascar]],<ref name="Yap 2017" /> and is now found across south east Asia.<ref name="Quattrocchi">{{cite book|last1=Quattrocchi|first1=Umberto|title=CRC World Dictionary of Medicinal and Poisonous Plants: Common Names, Scientific Names, Eponyms, Synonyms, and Etymology|date=2016|publisher=CRC Press|isbn=9781482250640|page=3587|chapter=Strobilanthes Blume Acanthaceae}}</ref> It is a member of the family [[Acanthaceae]].<ref name="Yap 2017" /> It is known as {{lang|zsm|pokok pecah kaca}} or {{lang|zsm|pokok pecah beling}} in [[Malaysia]],<ref name="Yap 2017" /> and {{lang|id|pecah beling}}, {{lang|id|enyoh kilo}}, {{lang|id|kecibeling}} or {{lang|id|kejibeling}} in [[Indonesia]].{{Citation needed|date=February 2018}} The leaves are used traditionally for treatment of cancer and diabetes,<ref name="Yap 2017">{{cite book|last1=Yap|first1=Ling-Sze|last2=Lee|first2=Wai-Leng|last3=Ting|first3=Adeline-Su-Yien|editor1-last=Agrawal|editor1-first=Dinesh Chandra|editor2-last=Tsay|editor2-first=Hsin-Sheng|editor3-last=Shyur|editor3-first=Lie-Fen|editor4-last=Wu|editor4-first=Yang-Chang|editor5-last=Wang|editor5-first=Sheng-Yang|title=Medicinal Plants and Fungi: Recent Advances in Research and Development|date=2017|publisher=Springer|isbn=9789811059780|page=328|chapter=Endophytes from Malaysian medicinal plants as sources for discovering anticancer agents}}</ref> usually taken as a tea or infusion of the leaves.<ref name="Quattrocchi"/>

